%I A401077 #28 Nov 11 2026 20:10:39
%S A401077 0,0,0,0,0,12514320,34395777360,32307576315840,17952208799918400
%N A401077 Number of n X n {0,1}-matrices of rank 5 over the real numbers.
%C A401077 Also the number of n X n {0,1}-matrices of rank 5 over the rational numbers.
%C A401077 Unlike the cases of rank k <= 2, where every k-dimensional subspace of R^n generated by {0,1}-vectors is spanned by a k X n {0,1}-matrix containing the k X k identity matrix I_k as a submatrix, for rank k >= 3 there exist k-dimensional {0,1}-subspaces whose reduced row echelon basis involves fractional entries (arising from k X k {0,1}-submatrices with |det| >= 2).
%H A401077 Miodrag Živković, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0511636">Classification of small (0,1) matrices</a>, arXiv:math/0511636 [math.CO], 2005; see Table 3, p. 19; Linear Algebra and its Applications, 414 (2006), 310-346, see Table 3, p. 324.
%e A401077 For n < 5, no n X n matrix can have rank 5, so a(0) = a(1) = a(2) = a(3) = a(4) = 0.
%e A401077 For n = 5, a(5) = 12514320 is the number of nonsingular 5 X 5 {0,1}-matrices over R.
%Y A401077 Column k=5 of A064230.
